From ece3f5d0109c05d8b8d12b125cd4e243f184e120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pauleveritt <pauleveritt@me.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:29:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] mellum: optimized q8 prefill and decode

Tiled expert GEMMs from 32 rows, batched Q8_0 projections, Metal 4
tensor-tile experts, prefill attention tiles with half operands, the four
decode fusions, and DS4_MELLUM_EXACT_PREFILL for diagnostics. The f32 tiled
attention experiment is removed, the sliding decode kernel loads two keys
before folding either, and its reference kernel ships for the comparison.

The A/B/B/A CLI runners, their model-free contract, the 2048-token decode
prompt and the three oracle token fixtures ship with the patch. The oracle
compares against an immutable d2d9338 build, each engine from its own tree.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: upstream has equivalent Mellum fast paths
